{
 "schema": "alpha_relevance_elements.v1",
 "status": "EXPERIMENTAL (P4 phase 1). Element content copied verbatim from the round-36 A9 v2 draft element ownership table (alpha_tier_element_ownership.v2) for alpha_taxonomy_v1; the taxonomy itself is not edited. Used only as the definition anchors of the alpha_relevance_judge task. Not approved, not gold, carries no weights.",
 "source_schema": "alpha_tier_element_ownership.v2",
 "source_sha256": "2e1ff9d1d587709a7d8322df4dc4cab0e43daeaac9ec5adaa7effcfd411a8da2",
 "taxonomy_content_version": "1.1.0",
 "rules": {
  "U1_unit": "The unit of judgment is the substantive VARIABLE (a named quantity, event or state) with direction, magnitude, comparison baseline and time stripped. A 'condition' list entry ('revenue accelerates') contributes its variable ('revenue'); a 'relation' entry ('stock falls despite earnings') is its own element of kind 'relation'.",
  "U2_heads": "Each list entry contributes its HEAD variable(s): the quantity whose state the entry asserts. Other variables that appear only as targets/baselines of the asserted relation are RELATA; relata never confer ownership.",
  "U3_relations": "A relation element is engaged only when the claim states the relation; stating a relatum alone does not engage it.",
  "U4_engaged_vs_mentioned": "ENGAGED: the claim's content is ABOUT the variable (asserts, reports, measures, forecasts, conditions on, negates, or asks about its state or change). MENTIONED: the name appears but the content is about something else (list label, denominator, adjective, qualifier, surface collision).",
  "identity": "Two list entries name the SAME element only if they name the same head quantity in the same domain (inflection, direction words, a literal synonym, or a specific/general pair of the same quantity are allowed). A measure, proxy, consequence or accumulation of a quantity is a DIFFERENT element ('orders' is not 'demand'; 'backlog' is not 'orders'; 'AI revenue' is not 'demand for accelerators'). Merges that involve a confirmation entry are tier-relevant and carry judgment=true when they are not literal; near-identical pairs deliberately NOT merged are recorded in related_not_merged with the tier that merging would produce.",
  "priority": "Q1-first (unchanged): an element is core-owned if it has a head occurrence in core_thesis, trigger_signals or invalidation_conditions; it is strong-eligible only if its head occurrences are all in confirmation_signals. A confirmation entry whose element is core-owned is SHADOWED: it can never produce 'strong'. Claim tier = highest tier among ENGAGED elements (core > strong); a claim that engages no element but mentions elements or uses topic terms is weak; otherwise none. 'moderate' has no closed set in the taxonomy and is UNDEFINED here."
 },
